WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.868 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You obviously can't watch
your stage work,

00:00:01.868 --> 00:00:03.336 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you could watch
your film work.

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:04.204 line:92%
But you do not like to do that.

00:00:04.204 --> 00:00:06.172 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right, well, 'cause
I'm used to doing plays.

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:09.743 align:start size:94% position:6%
I came from
a theater background.

00:00:09.743 --> 00:00:11.044 line:92%
So it never really equated to me

00:00:11.044 --> 00:00:12.679 align:start size:94% position:6%
that why would I want
to watch that.

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:16.616
So long as I know what it feels
like, that's good enough for me.

00:00:16.616 --> 00:00:19.919
-But then it was problematic
because you were an actual

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:21.654 line:92%
"Star Wars" fan, so you then --

00:00:21.654 --> 00:00:24.858 align:start size:94% position:6%
Could you not watch the new
"Star Wars" movies?

00:00:24.858 --> 00:00:26.359 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-I did. I did. I did.

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:28.495 line:92%
Well, because also, I mean --

00:00:28.495 --> 00:00:30.630
Defend myself 'cause all my
friends afterwards, like,

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:32.699
"You didn't watch our movie,
but you watched 'Star Wars.'"

00:00:32.699 --> 00:00:35.402
But you're standing in front of
the screen, and they're like,

00:00:35.402 --> 00:00:36.803 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Trust us.
Your lightsaber is working."

00:00:36.803 --> 00:00:40.340 align:start size:94% position:6%
"There's space behind you.
It looks really cool."

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:44.811
So when you're, like, just
standing in a rainy backlot,

00:00:44.811 --> 00:00:46.546
it doesn't seem very impressive.
-Yeah.

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:49.215 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You don't feel like
you're commanding anybody

00:00:49.215 --> 00:00:52.485 align:start size:94% position:6%
other than sticks
and ping-pong balls.

00:00:52.485 --> 00:00:54.587 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:54.587 --> 00:00:55.755 size:81% position:41% line:92%
I did once go to a set

00:00:55.755 --> 00:00:57.690
that was green screen,
and I was really excited.

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:59.626 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I had this real moment
where I was like,

00:00:59.626 --> 00:01:00.727 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, I'm not
supposed to be here."

00:01:00.727 --> 00:01:03.396 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just watching a really good
actor act with, like,

00:01:03.396 --> 00:01:05.732 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, a tennis ball
on a stick, you're like --

00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:07.801 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"I have this in my basement."
-Yeah.

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:11.504
"I could just watch 'Star Wars'
in my basement now."

00:01:11.504 --> 00:01:12.172 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"BlacKkKlansman."

00:01:12.172 --> 00:01:13.473 align:start size:94% position:6%
Congratulations
on your nomination.

00:01:13.473 --> 00:01:15.909
-Oh, thank you very much.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:15.909 --> 00:01:17.877 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-I know that that --

00:01:17.877 --> 00:01:19.979 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, when that premieres
at Cannes,

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:22.215 line:92%
do you skip that out, too?

00:01:22.215 --> 00:01:25.151
Like, I mean, obviously,
you're invited to the premiere.

00:01:25.151 --> 00:01:26.386 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes, yeah.

00:01:26.386 --> 00:01:28.488 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, Cannes is very like --
They're very --

00:01:28.488 --> 00:01:31.991
I don't want to say serious,
because you're kind of like,

00:01:31.991 --> 00:01:33.726 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Yeah, films are
this important."

00:01:33.726 --> 00:01:35.962 align:start size:94% position:6%
You, like, walk up this, like,
kind of sacrificial steps

00:01:35.962 --> 00:01:39.599
like you're going to kill a goat
together or something.

00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:41.501 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then everyone goes in,
and we watch a movie.

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:43.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
But you have to be back
'cause the lights come up,

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:48.675 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then they put the camera
where you were sitting.

00:01:48.675 --> 00:01:50.810 align:start size:94% position:6%
And if you're not there,
it looks bad.

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:52.145 size:88% position:44% line:92%
So I just go into a room

00:01:52.145 --> 00:01:56.316 size:88% position:44%
and then wait, you know,
with a guy in silence.

00:01:56.316 --> 00:01:58.751 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, you know,
"Okay, now I got to go back

00:01:58.751 --> 00:02:01.588
and sneak in and pretend like
I was there the whole time."

00:02:01.588 --> 00:02:03.289 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, I get not wanting
to watch yourself.

00:02:03.289 --> 00:02:05.492 align:start size:94% position:6%
But being willing to do
the other -- I mean, like,

00:02:05.492 --> 00:02:06.526 align:start size:94% position:6%
going out to dinner
is one thing,

00:02:06.526 --> 00:02:08.561
but, like, going in a room
with a stranger, I feel like...

00:02:08.561 --> 00:02:10.964
You should just try to push
through and watch the movie.

00:02:10.964 --> 00:02:14.801
-I know. Yeah, I guess that does
sound really bleak.

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:17.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
It always seems like a better
alternative than watching

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:19.139 align:start size:94% position:6%
all the mistakes
that you're making

00:02:19.139 --> 00:02:20.874 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's now immortalized
on film forever.

00:02:20.874 --> 00:02:23.843 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. Real quick,
because you mentioned

00:02:23.843 --> 00:02:24.911 line:92%
Arts in the Armed Forces.

00:02:24.911 --> 00:02:27.780
We've talked before about
your military background.

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.549 align:start size:94% position:6%
How many years now running
is this?

00:02:29.549 --> 00:02:31.684 size:84% position:42%
-Ten years. We've been
doing it for ten years.

00:02:31.684 --> 00:02:33.253 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's amazing.
-Yeah, thank you.

00:02:33.253 --> 00:02:34.521 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:34.521 --> 00:02:35.922 line:92%
-And I assume you keep doing it

00:02:35.922 --> 00:02:38.791 align:start size:94% position:6%
because you're getting
such good feedback.

00:02:38.791 --> 00:02:39.626 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Is it growing, as well?

00:02:39.626 --> 00:02:41.294 align:start size:94% position:6%
Are you getting out
to more people?

00:02:41.294 --> 00:02:44.264
-Yeah, when we started, we were
still students at Juilliard,

00:02:44.264 --> 00:02:46.466 size:84% position:42%
and we were doing it,
like, in our apartment.

00:02:46.466 --> 00:02:49.736 align:start size:94% position:6%
Handtyping, you know,
on a typewriter

00:02:49.736 --> 00:02:51.905 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause we thought
that was very cool.

00:02:51.905 --> 00:02:52.772 line:92%
Thank-you notes to people.

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:54.741 align:start size:94% position:6%
We had enough for
one performance a year.

00:02:54.741 --> 00:02:57.710 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's all we could do
while we were still students.

00:02:57.710 --> 00:02:59.946 align:start size:94% position:6%
And now we have
incredible donors,

00:02:59.946 --> 00:03:02.549
and we're doing 15 performances
already this year.

00:03:02.549 --> 00:03:05.418 align:start size:94% position:6%
We just came back
from Fort Leavenworth.

00:03:05.418 --> 00:03:07.020 line:92%
And we have, like, branched out

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:10.290 align:start size:94% position:6%
and have done
this playwrighting grant --

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:12.926 align:start size:94% position:6%
$10,000 to anyone in
the military to write a play

00:03:12.926 --> 00:03:14.460 align:start size:94% position:6%
about anything,
about ping-pong balls.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:17.397 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-I know I'm referencing you.

00:03:17.397 --> 00:03:18.731 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I'm that guy.

00:03:18.731 --> 00:03:22.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So we're kind of exploring
what the whole arts --

00:03:22.068 --> 00:03:24.971 align:start size:94% position:6%
Not just theater,
but we'll still do, you know,

00:03:24.971 --> 00:03:27.440 align:start size:94% position:6%
have, like, this
traveling troupe of actors

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:29.008 size:88% position:44% line:92%
that go around the world

00:03:29.008 --> 00:03:32.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
performing for military
audiences, either veterans,

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:36.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
servicemen and women and their
families, at any base or --

00:03:36.649 --> 00:03:38.985 align:start size:94% position:6%
We do an annual performance
on Broadway every year.

00:03:38.985 --> 00:03:40.220 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's great.
Thanks for doing that.

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:43.323
And thanks for being here, man.
It's always such a pleasure.

00:03:43.323 --> 00:03:45.625 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Really appreciate it.

